Adapted material

qsmsim/rc2.py contains a Python port of the evaluation code of the QSM
Reconstruction Challenge 2.0 (functions4challenge/evaluation/:
EvaluateRecon_ChallengeFinalMetrics.m and _vs2.m, compute_rmse_detrend_v1.m,
compute_linearityDeepGM.m, compute_calcification_metrics_v0.m / _v2.m,
dilatemask.m, Combine_ChallengeSim1Sim2Metrics.m), from

  "QSM Reconstruction Challenge 2.0 - Data and Code Provided to Participants",
  Zenodo, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4559541

by the QSM Challenge 2.0 organizers, licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
Changes: translated from MATLAB to Python/NumPy, indices mapped from 1-based
inclusive ranges to 0-based slices, LPS headers reoriented as MATLAB's load_nii
does, and the stage-1 and vs2 variants selected by an argument.

Challenge papers:
  Marques JP, Meineke J, Milovic C, Bilgic B, et al. QSM reconstruction
  challenge 2.0: A realistic in silico head phantom for MRI data simulation and
  evaluation of susceptibility mapping procedures. Magn Reson Med.
  2021;86:526-542. https://doi.org/10.1002/mrm.28716
  QSM Challenge 2.0 Organization Committee: Bilgic B, Langkammer C, Marques JP,
  Meineke J, Milovic C, Schweser F. QSM reconstruction challenge 2.0: Design and
  report of results. Magn Reson Med. 2021;86:1241-1255.
  https://doi.org/10.1002/mrm.28754

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data not included

Phantom P3 is built at run time from the challenge's Sim1 head (CC-BY 4.0),
which qsmsim-fetch-rc2 downloads from the challenge's public share. Those data
are not redistributed here; qsmsim/exp1/rc2_sha256.json only lists their
checksums. Cite the papers above when you use P3.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reimplemented methods

The field-mapping, background-removal and dipole-inversion methods (SHARP,
V-SHARP, PDF, LBV, TKD, CF-L2, TV-ADMM, the MEDI-like morphology prior, TFI)
were written from their published descriptions, cited in each module; no code
from the original authors' toolboxes is included. The optional cross-check in
qsmsim/qsmjl.py and julia/ calls QSM.jl (MIT License,
https://github.com/kamesy/QSM.jl) as an external package; it is not bundled.
